## Important Notes

{% if manage_route_table %}
- **Route table import is mandatory** — see *Route Table Management* above.
  Skipping it will destroy and recreate the default route table, breaking
  existing connectivity.
- **Always run `terraform state show` after import** to capture all pre-existing
  routes before the first `terraform apply`.
- **Stop if you see `-` in the plan** on any existing `route_rules` block — a
  production route is about to be deleted. Add the missing rule before applying.
{% else %}
- **Route tables are not managed by Terraform** in this configuration — no
  `terraform import` is needed. Add the DG route rule manually after apply.
- **Always read existing rules before updating** via the CLI — the OCI API
  replaces the entire `route-rules` array on each update, not just appends.
{% endif %}
- **Same-region only** — this module uses Local Peering Gateways. For
  cross-region Data Guard, use the Cross-Region configuration which provisions
  DRGs and Remote Peering Connections.
- **Teardown** — `terraform destroy` removes the LPGs and NSG rules.
  Route table OCIDs remain intact; any manually added DG route rules
  must also be removed manually.
